# Leave DATABASE_URL unset to use embedded PGlite (zero-setup local Postgres).
# Set it to a Neon connection string for deployed environments.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@ep-xxx.neon.tech/loya?sslmode=require
AUTH_SECRET=change-me-in-production
POS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=demo-secret

# --- WhatsApp via OpenWA (see docs/integration-openwa-whatsapp.md) ---
# All three required to enable the "openwa" ESP provider and WhatsApp
# blast campaigns (src/modules/blast). OpenWA runs as its own always-on
# service — not part of this deployment — see the OpenWA repo's own
# docs/local-dev-sandbox-notes.md for how to stand it up and pair a
# session. Leave all three unset to run without WhatsApp (default).
# OPENWA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:2785
# OPENWA_API_KEY=owa_k1_...              # an OPERATOR-role key scoped to OPENWA_SESSION_ID only
# OPENWA_SESSION_ID=your-session-id      # a session already paired to a real WhatsApp number

# HMAC secret for inbound OpenWA webhook deliveries (src/app/api/whatsapp/
# webhook/route.ts) — set this on both sides when registering the webhook
# via OpenWA's POST /api/sessions/:sessionId/webhooks. If left unset, the
# route accepts unsigned requests (fine for local dev only — see the
# route's own comment for why this is enforced once a secret exists).
# OPENWA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional: powers the "Generate draft" button on the blast composer
# (src/modules/blast/generate-content.ts). Without it, the button is
# simply hidden — blasts still work with manually-written copy.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
